  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "One clock",
      "items": [
        "A night lasts about ninety seconds, and every third one is a storm",
        "The same clock sets the palette, the difficulty and the music, so dawn arrives at once",
        "Dawn is a transition, not a cut: the sky drains back into dusk rather than going black"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Made, not loaded",
      "items": [
        "The sky is a fragment shader; there is no sky image anywhere",
        "The music is generated — chords, drums and a lead over a pentatonic scale",
        "The map has no tiles: meadows, rifts and currents are functions of where you are"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Kept and shared",
      "items": [
        "Keys, learned abilities and caught phrases live in the browser and survive a death",
        "The chronicle is a Cloudflare worker over KV, with a plain node twin for a box of one's own",
        "Only a run's best is recorded, and a password is stored salted and hashed, never itself"
      ]
    }
  ]
